<title>USA: US chain store sales fell 1.2 pct - BTM/Schroders.</title>
<headline>US chain store sales fell 1.2 pct - BTM/Schroders.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. chain store sales fell 1.2 percent in the week ended September 28 from the prior week, according to the seasonally adjusted BTM/Schroders weekly chain store sales index.</p>
<p>Sales for the week were up 2.6 percent on a year-over-year basis, while the month-to-date index slipped 1.1 percent from the prior month.</p>
<p>&quot;The lastest week's sales were generally below plan for most retailers with the discount segment of the business particularly weak,&quot; a BTM/Schroders report said.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1562</p>
</text>
